The two files in this directory are VENDORED VERBATIM from HuggingFace
Transformers and are licensed Apache-2.0, not AGPL-3.0. Their original
copyright headers are intact and must stay that way.

    modeling_qwen4_exp.py
    configuration_qwen4_exp.py

    from: https://github.com/huggingface/transformers
          src/transformers/models/qwen4_exp/
    at:   transformers 5.8.0.dev0 (the revision the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next
          transcriptions in this repo were read against)

WHY A COPY EXISTS, given that nothing imports it.

Every golden generator here — `hc_golden.py`, `ple_golden.py`, `qsa_golden.py`,
`forward_ref.py`, `slice_ref.py` — imports from the INSTALLED `transformers`
package, so this directory could be deleted without breaking a test or a
generator. It is kept for two reasons:

  1. The transcriptions cite it by LINE NUMBER (for example
     `kernels/gb10/qwen3.8-flash-next/nvfp4/ple.cu` cites
     `modeling_qwen4_exp.py L1168` for the PLE forward). A citation into a
     moving upstream file stops resolving; a citation into a pinned copy does
     not.
  2. The generators now run against `transformers` 5.16.1 while the
     transcriptions were made against 5.8.0.dev0. This copy is the only record
     of the text that was actually transcribed, which is what an argument about
     a numerical disagreement would need.

So the copy is documentation of provenance, not a dependency. If it is ever
dropped, the line-number citations should become revision-pinned URLs in the
same change.

HOW THIS DIFFERS FROM `bench/ngram_embed/LICENSE`. That notice covers an
INDEPENDENT DERIVATION — no upstream file vendored, the MIT notice travelling
with the derivation because it is close enough to the published implementation.
This one covers actual vendored files, so Apache-2.0 applies to them directly.

The Rust in `crates/` is not a transliteration of these files and remains
AGPL-3.0-only; `docs/porting/QWEN4_EXP.md` carries the attribution for the
mechanisms derived from them.

Note on scope: `.licenserc.yaml` checks `crates/**/*.rs` and `kernels/**` only,
so nothing here is stamped with an Atlas SPDX header, and nothing should be.

